            <ArticleTitle>Pain: its experience, assessment and management in children.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>42-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This paper reviews the literature on pain assessment in children and in so doing indicates how the pain experiences of infants and children can be understood, assessed and effectively managed, even though those in pain may not have the vocabulary or ability to describe verbally such phenomena.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
